elemental mapping images of the ANCS catalyst.</p></div></div></div><div id="fig3" content-id="fig3" class="fig fig-modal reveal-modal" data-reveal="data-reveal"><div class="fig-label fig-label">Figure 3</div><div class="graphic-wrap"><a class="fig-link" href="/view-large/figure/165496536/ao4c03987_0003.tif" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" aria-describedby="sr-fig-viewer-action"><img class="content-image js-graphic-position-float" src="https://acs.silverchair-cdn.com/acs/content_public/journal/acsodf/9/33/10.1021_acsomega.4c03987/3/m_ao4c03987_0003.png?Expires=1791347537&amp;Signature=KgjWYr1K~IIjLZHg68JLIYKa4K0G6Q6nf8-jOI4U9-wqEv21GT1mF7jVuobqMLwbM1tQcT4m~xj7ZaKD0wJ8MBhstX0VfyU5hRbqqhAe-uKsv0z~~SGDRTbZlyu~Od0ruVbu5vy~KjRr8VQg8FWsKwkdWBWNHo~Bnepjt8c5D9TkdkJhm0CBpP7xv-uRnxFuEtCCc81JjReR27C983xb2FRCJqJdwvPu2tSO6GP5nyVCFPWWk5~PG5QxTjYZnC9JGrXdqdaM85RX45~YMo1rntQeURZG3Nlj6Rtr9duz1y8YKzK4VeuScQpwj9Rr62ttTYgpPeDnpiydbCpwYlrA4w__&amp;Key-Pair-Id=APKAIE5G5CRDK6RD3PGA" data-src="https://acs.silverchair-cdn.com/acs/content_public/journal/acsodf/9/33/10.1021_acsomega.4c03987/3/m_ao4c03987_0003.png?Expires=1791347537&amp;Signature=KgjWYr1K~IIjLZHg68JLIYKa4K0G6Q6nf8-jOI4U9-wqEv21GT1mF7jVuobqMLwbM1tQcT4m~xj7ZaKD0wJ8MBhstX0VfyU5hRbqqhAe-uKsv0z~~SGDRTbZlyu~Od0ruVbu5vy~KjRr8VQg8FWsKwkdWBWNHo~Bnepjt8c5D9TkdkJhm0CBpP7xv-uRnxFuEtCCc81JjReR27C983xb2FRCJqJdwvPu2tSO6GP5nyVCFPWWk5~PG5QxTjYZnC9JGrXdqdaM85RX45~YMo1rntQeURZG3Nlj6Rtr9duz1y8YKzK4VeuScQpwj9Rr62ttTYgpPeDnpiydbCpwYlrA4w__&amp;Key-Pair-Id=APKAIE5G5CRDK6RD3PGA" alt="Figure 3. Refer to the image caption for details." path-from-xml="ao4c03987_0003.tif" /></a><div class="fig-orig original-slide"><a section="165496536" class="fig-view-orig at-figureViewLarge" role="button" href="/view-large/figure/165496536/ao4c03987_0003.tif" path-from-xml="ao4c03987_0003.tif" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" aria-label="View large Figure 3.">View Large</a><a section="165496536" href="//acs.silverchair-cdn.com/DownloadFile/DownloadImage.aspx?image=https://acs.silverchair-cdn.com/acs/content_public/journal/acsodf/9/33/10.1021_acsomega.4c03987/3/ao4c03987_0003.png?Expires=1791347537&Signature=Zee7pLkxYevFkLA0X1q8nwMIUDPG2faS-LVbo3mMxp7xP4J-qTnVSMIP4F-OZZUcHvbMpyhsdInvfDXO-UjsDfSoVSkxHhQJUMiFj40hUX2kQZieJ9EVpUsB7Lhu418WijBZfn-OyfdPnPeZVPKN3PCBMkQSalYj6GHcLGkZ2JCWnjydnrk~GTQkmQdfMUIw8ZHSGxVv7RWkKFpB147-cynMaCg3bwE07YmJRo1jZES~-PBLMcleCha7v3dbrNu9ZsKfgf~I5N0RwtMjUxsc7AGyRIpBJmCLL4Rj9821EqWiP-AWf8PgzBvqJkR9NK4xjueG9iuFfJHaHyKpPfHVbw__&Key-Pair-Id=APKAIE5G5CRDK6RD3PGA&sec=165496536&ar=358560&xsltPath=~/UI/app/XSLT&imagename=&siteId=1000073" class="download-slide stats-download-slide js-download-file-gtm-datalayer-event" role="button" data-filetype="ppt" path-from-xml="ao4c03987_0003.tif" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" aria-label="Download slide for Figure 3.">Download to Slide</a></div></div><div class="graphic-bottom"><div class="label fig-label">Figure 3.</div><div class="caption fig-caption"><p>STEM-EDAX
elemental mapping images of the ANCS catalyst.</p></div></div><a class="close-reveal-modal" href="javascript:;"><i class="icon-general-close" aria-hidden="true"> </i><span class="screenreader-text">Close Figure 3.</span></a></div>
                </div>
                <div id="165496537-content" class="article-section-wrapper js-article-section js-content-section  " data-section-parent-id="165496533">
                    
                    <p>The powder XRD data showed a broad diffraction peak at 2 theta
of 25.2° in the CS sample, which belongs to the (002) plane of
the graphene sheets (<a href="javascript:;" reveal-id="fig4" data-open="fig4" class="link link-reveal link-table xref-fig">Figure 4</a>a).  (<a href="javascript:;" ref-data-modal-source-id="ref29" class="link link-ref xref-bibr js-link-ref">29</a>,<a href="javascript:;" ref-data-modal-source-id="ref30" class="link link-ref xref-bibr js-link-ref">30</a>) The broadness of the graphitic
(002) plane was increased in ACS and ANCS samples, which is due to
the increased defects along with variation in the interlayer stacking
of the graphene sheets due to the KOH activation and N-doping. The
ACS and ANCS samples show an additional broad XRD peak at 2 theta
of 43.7°, corresponding to the (100) plane of the graphitic structure.
The Raman spectra of all the samples showed two bands at 1349 and
1589 cm<sup>–1</sup>, which belong to the defective (D) and
graphitic (G) nature of the carbon, respectively (<a href="javascript:;" reveal-id="fig4" data-open="fig4" class="link link-reveal link-table xref-fig">Figure 4</a>b).  (<a href="javascript:;" ref-data-modal-source-id="ref31" class="link link-ref xref-bibr js-link-ref">31</a>,<a href="javascript:;" ref-data-modal-source-id="ref32" class="link link-ref xref-bibr js-link-ref">32</a>) The defective D band can denote disordered carbon, structural defects,
and/or the defunctionalization of oxygen-based species in carbon materials.
The <em>I</em><sub>D</sub>/<em>I</em><sub>G</sub> ratio
represents the relative number of defect sites in the carbon framework.
The ANCS sample contains a higher ratio of <em>I</em><sub>D</sub>/<em>I</em><sub>G</sub> (1.53) in comparison to the
ACS (1.26) and CS (0.86) samples. This is due to the replacement of
carbon atoms in the graphitic structure with nitrogen atoms, forming
nitrogen-based functional groups with disordered carbon and structural
defects in the ANCS sample, which was elucidated by FT-IR, EPR, and
XPS analyses in the following sections.</p>
                </div>
                <div id="165496538-content" class="article-section-wrapper js-article-section js-content-section  " data-section-parent-id="165496533">
                    
