le/DownloadImage.aspx?image=https://acs.silverchair-cdn.com/acs/content_public/journal/acsodf/9/33/10.1021_acsomega.4c03987/3/ao4c03987_0004.png?Expires=1791347537&Signature=CBuxz2zb0tobslTm74GANdfP23qsc-pHlJ9QfVRN0ehhjvx1uNz0CVRrE7JLbhdNxMAFVHt3Ktky2zXTmXDaH~j6Ju-gXBCXxglQAj-2wI0U~S4pakPU63wtT~rKVvWF7ISgSyNYcWPH19w05nSem2kZa8c0ghSF3s3mCcQzPhIh6-ZFgvOK75-rqf5oPAw6lDE7bbAH5eReZrjPgBAiK76CGHddETU~oolRPG7DiMdPGdXXL2EOGxVvqTfHZ5PlyGk64ICcw9rL30XDtens~minwEjLQkxA372XsezkODPtsgoJ7igzSNnlQRLSp4pSOsFVRVvXqCYmSNg88ECtBA__&Key-Pair-Id=APKAIE5G5CRDK6RD3PGA&sec=165496538&ar=358560&xsltPath=~/UI/app/XSLT&imagename=&siteId=1000073" class="download-slide stats-download-slide js-download-file-gtm-datalayer-event" role="button" data-filetype="ppt" path-from-xml="ao4c03987_0004.tif" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" aria-label="Download slide for Figure 4.">Download to Slide</a></div></div><div class="graphic-bottom"><div class="label fig-label">Figure 4.</div><div class="caption fig-caption"><p>(a) Powder XRD patterns
and (b) Raman spectra of candle soot (CS),
activated candle soot (ACS), and activated N-doped candle soot (ANCS)
catalysts.</p></div></div></div><div id="fig4" content-id="fig4" class="fig fig-modal reveal-modal" data-reveal="data-reveal"><div class="fig-label fig-label">Figure 4</div><div class="graphic-wrap"><a class="fig-link" href="/view-large/figure/165496538/ao4c03987_0004.tif" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" aria-describedby="sr-fig-viewer-action"><img class="content-image js-graphic-position-float" src="https://acs.silverchair-cdn.com/acs/content_public/journal/acsodf/9/33/10.1021_acsomega.4c03987/3/m_ao4c03987_0004.png?Expires=1791347537&amp;Signature=GAKYPcX9pzlMikcPF0e7u2tfl7xx2X3Fdh1O4ehnC9xTiyvaFT9MDGStdmRlVkRcqmaMsZFc46g7JN8w~52qnEskiM5Nv-RXM8BEp9xNhqrXL27gsl4EazXPA916oSD~GYPy2TEJg33KH9fXTY6qm2qxW5eQWWYz8uzl77WL2ZPY6r1JZ63Bp4~d2LPVadH0g1nDv4OqMsSFjmuTYMq0V7ALkMbM9yO9iJd2WTDVl5ZgdfhhEUfBDvaN0VpOZIY85P07c6KSQKeh3qoypxka9D6e-qkqIFD2mAggfkbLLlo6qHTQ3nqeh7ahNA8ES9qNE8xSvCezke4iFahzdK0EUA__&amp;Key-Pair-Id=APKAIE5G5CRDK6RD3PGA" data-src="https://acs.silverchair-cdn.com/acs/content_public/journal/acsodf/9/33/10.1021_acsomega.4c03987/3/m_ao4c03987_0004.png?Expires=1791347537&amp;Signature=GAKYPcX9pzlMikcPF0e7u2tfl7xx2X3Fdh1O4ehnC9xTiyvaFT9MDGStdmRlVkRcqmaMsZFc46g7JN8w~52qnEskiM5Nv-RXM8BEp9xNhqrXL27gsl4EazXPA916oSD~GYPy2TEJg33KH9fXTY6qm2qxW5eQWWYz8uzl77WL2ZPY6r1JZ63Bp4~d2LPVadH0g1nDv4OqMsSFjmuTYMq0V7ALkMbM9yO9iJd2WTDVl5ZgdfhhEUfBDvaN0VpOZIY85P07c6KSQKeh3qoypxka9D6e-qkqIFD2mAggfkbLLlo6qHTQ3nqeh7ahNA8ES9qNE8xSvCezke4iFahzdK0EUA__&amp;Key-Pair-Id=APKAIE5G5CRDK6RD3PGA" alt="Figure 4. Refer to the image caption for details." path-from-xml="ao4c03987_0004.tif" /></a><div class="fig-orig original-slide"><a section="165496538" class="fig-view-orig at-figureViewLarge" role="button" href="/view-large/figure/165496538/ao4c03987_0004.tif" path-from-xml="ao4c03987_0004.tif" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" aria-label="View large Figure 4.">View Large</a><a section="165496538" href="//acs.silverchair-cdn.com/DownloadFile/DownloadImage.aspx?image=https://acs.silverchair-cdn.com/acs/content_public/journal/acsodf/9/33/10.1021_acsomega.4c03987/3/ao4c03987_0004.png?Expires=1791347537&Signature=CBuxz2zb0tobslTm74GANdfP23qsc-pHlJ9QfVRN0ehhjvx1uNz0CVRrE7JLbhdNxMAFVHt3Ktky2zXTmXDaH~j6Ju-gXBCXxglQAj-2wI0U~S4pakPU63wtT~rKVvWF7ISgSyNYcWPH19w05nSem2kZa8c0ghSF3s3mCcQzPhIh6-ZFgvOK75-rqf5oPAw6lDE7bbAH5eReZrjPgBAiK76CGHddETU~oolRPG7DiMdPGdXXL2EOGxVvqTfHZ5PlyGk64ICcw9rL30XDtens~minwEjLQkxA372XsezkODPtsgoJ7igzSNnlQRLSp4pSOsFVRVvXqCYmSNg88ECtBA__&Key-Pair-Id=APKAIE5G5CRDK6RD3PGA&sec=165496538&ar=358560&xsltPath=~/UI/app/XSLT&imagename=&siteId=1000073" class="download-slide stats-download-slide js-download-file-gtm-datalayer-event" role="button" data-filetype="ppt" path-from-xml="ao4c03987_0004.tif" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" aria-label="Download slide for Figure 4.">Download to Slide</a></div></div><div class="graphic-bottom"><div class="label fig-label">Figure 4.</div><div class="caption fig-caption"><p>(a) Powder XRD patterns
and (b) Raman spectra of candle soot (CS),
activated candle soot (ACS), and activated N-doped candle soot (ANCS)
catalysts.</p></div></div><a class="close-reveal-modal" href="javascript:;"><i class="icon-general-close" aria-hidden="true"> </i><span class="screenreader-text">Close Figure 4.</span></a></div>
                </div>
                <div id="165496539-content" class="article-section-wrapper js-article-section js-content-section  " data-section-parent-id="165496533">
                    
                    <p>The FT-IR analysis was conducted
to identify the functional groups
in the carbon materials (<a href="javascript:;" reveal-id="fig5" data-open="fig5" class="link link-reveal link-table xref-fig">Figure 5</a>a). All the samples exhibit a broad peak in the range
3300–3500 cm<sup>–1</sup> belonging to functional hydroxyl
(−OH) and/or amine (−NH) groups. The pure CS sample
shows several peaks belonging to −C–O (1238 cm<sup>–1</sup>), −C=C (1596 cm<sup>–1</sup>), −COOH/–C=O
(1730 cm<sup>–1</sup>), and −OH (3418 cm<sup>–1</sup>) groups.  (<a href="javascript:;" ref-data-modal-source-id="ref26" class="link link-ref xref-bibr js-link-ref">26</a>,<a href="javascript:;" ref-data-modal-source-id="ref33" class="link link-ref xref-bibr js-link-ref">33</a>) These peaks are not found in
the ACS sample, which is due to the removal of oxygen-containing groups
by KOH activation. In the place of oxygen functional groups, various
N-based functional groups (−C–N; 1144 cm<sup>–1</sup>, −C=N; 1587 cm<sup>–1</sup>, and −NH; 3449
cm<sup>–1</sup>) were noticed in the ANCS sample, indicating
the N-doping in the carbon structure, in line with the Raman studies
(<a href="javascript:;" reveal-id="fig4" data-open="fig4" class="link link-reveal link-table xref-fig">Figure 4</a>b). An FT-IR
peak corresponding to the aromatic methyl group (−CH; 593 cm<sup>–1</sup>) is observed only in the case of the ANCS sample.  (<a href="javascript:;" ref-data-modal-source-id="ref26" class="link link-ref xref-bibr js-link-ref">26</a>,<a href="javascript:;" ref-data-modal-source-id="ref33" class="link link-ref xref-bibr js-link-ref">33</a>) The EPR analysis showed that the ACS and ANCS catalysts exhibit
broader EPR signals and lower <em>g</em>-values as compared
to the pure CS catalyst (<a class="supplementary-material-link" reveal-id="all-supplement-materials-popup" data-open="all-supplement-materials-popup" href="/acsodf/article-supplement/358560/pdf/ao4c03987_si_001/" path-from-xml="sifile1">Figure S2</a>, Supporting
Information). This indicates the perturbations in the electronic and
surface structure of the carbon framework after the KOH and N-doping
treatments.  (<a href="javascript:;" ref-data-modal-source-id="ref34" class="link link-ref xref-bibr js-link-ref">34</a>,<a href="javascript:;" ref-data-modal-source-id="ref35" class="link link-ref xref-bibr js-link-ref">35</a>) A decrease in the <em>g</em>-value of the ACS and ANCS catalysts compared to the pure CS catalyst
indicates a decrease in the degree of oxidation of the carbon in ACS
and ANCS catalysts. The increased width of the EPR peaks reveals an
increased BET surface area of ACS and ANCS catalysts compared to the
CS catalyst (<a class="supplementary-material-link" reveal-id="all-supplement-materials-popup" data-open="all-supplement-materials-popup" href="/acsodf/article-supplement/358560/pdf/ao4c03987_si_001/" path-from-xml="sifile1">Table S1</a>, Supporting Information). (<a href="javascript:;" ref-data-modal-source-id="ref35" class="link link-ref xref-bibr js-link-ref">35</a>) Though the EPR analysis is used to estimate
the defect density in the carbon materials, it must be indicated that
the EPR technique cannot detect all defects present in the carbon
framework. (<a href="javascript:;" ref-data-modal-source-id="ref34" class="link link-ref xref-bibr js-link-ref">34</a>)</p>
                </div>
                <div id="165496540-content" class="article-section-wrapper js-article-section js-content-section  " data-section-parent-id="165496533">
                    
                    <a id = "165496540" scrollto-destination="165496540"></a><div data-id="fig5" class="fig fig-section" reveal-group-id="sec3.1"><span class="hidden" id="viewTranscriptId_"></span><div class="fig-label fig-label">Figure 5</div><div class="graphic-wrap"><a class="fig-link" href="/view-large/figure/165496540/ao4c03987_0005.tif" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" aria-describedby="sr-fig-viewer-action"><img class="content-image js-graphic-position-float" src="https://acs.silverchair-cdn.com/acs/content_public/journal/acsodf/9/33/10.1021_acsomega.4c03987/3/m_ao4c03987_0005.png?Expires=1791347537&amp;Signature=eBv9jXhyvPOxKHF4hwnRkmwirgH0TOLbZJM1rYi-8lDK67o3vHUm04MAC-lBgAfvyZrv5GgsTowtQC6N3isXjKxS0HZCWpqmsic0afomjQFR~rYrXG7EpfVDnFbeA45uelFef961aSFFo5tyQUcdR1mG59lI-k12vuZd706DLJJX-jpXDxSwRusFqqTyahOi-3BQCu5olgKgvb-50q0YkQZWoh2GNGhtQkTdl4AIrcZb2DYkM1is5XAdxlcABn~iLSfjvD6UYiBD0KBJx5nDZKxJHlr~W5OcLZuhtrfrTlaoRPr6Fz~dR0D4qKIqvGU4OiZduJH-n53MV750YXmPRw__&amp;Key-Pair-Id=APKAIE5G5CRDK6RD3PGA" data-src="https://acs.silverchair-cdn.com/acs/content_public/journal/acsodf/9/33/10.1021_acsomega.4c03987/3/m_ao4c03987_0005.png?Expires=1791347537&amp;Signature=eBv9jXhyvPOxKHF4hwnRkmwirgH0TOLbZJM1rYi-8lDK67o3vHUm04MAC-lBgAfvyZrv5GgsTowtQC6N3isXjKxS0HZCWpqmsic0afomjQFR~rYrXG7EpfVDnFbeA45uelFef961aSFFo5tyQUcdR1mG59lI-k12vuZd706DLJJX-jpXDxSwRusFqqTyahOi-3BQCu5olgKgvb-50q0YkQZWoh2GNGhtQkTdl4AIrcZb2DYkM1is5XAdxlcABn~iLSfjvD6UYiBD0KBJx5nDZKxJHlr~W5OcLZuhtrfrTlaoRPr6Fz~dR0D4qKIqvGU4OiZduJH-n53MV750YXmPRw__&amp;Key-Pair-Id=APKAIE5G5CRDK6RD3PGA" alt="Figure 5. Refer to the image caption for details." path-from-xml="ao4c03987_0005.tif" /></a><div class="fig-orig original-slide"><a section="165496540" class="fig-view-orig at-figureViewLarge" role="button" href="/view-large/figure/165496540/ao4c03987_0005.tif" path-from-xml="ao4c03987_0005.tif" target="_blank" rel="nofollow" aria-label="View large Figure 5.">View Large</a><a section="165496540" href="//acs.silverchair-cdn.com/DownloadFi